==================== fn ====================
MAGI diagnosis  --  d = 325, p = 3, 18.0 s, no sampling

  check                           value     required         what it measures
  --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  distance to the mode          1.1e-03      < 1e-02   OK    sqrt(g' H^-1 g): how far this point is from the
                                                               true mode, in posterior sd. Unitless, so it
                                                               means the same across problems and dtypes
  gradient norm                 2.6e-03           --   info  the raw ||grad log p||, for reference. It carries
                                                               units and its floor is set by the working
                                                               precision, so it is not thresholded here
  negative curvature                  0            0   OK    directions in which the mode is a saddle, not a
                                                               maximum; a Gaussian there does not exist
  null directions                     0            0   OK    flat directions of the SCALED Hessian, so this is
                                                               unit-free; see the parameter table for which
  condition number              4.4e+03      < 1e+12   OK    of the scaled Hessian; beyond this the Laplace
                                                               covariance is not numerically meaningful
  curvature variation           3.8e+02      < 1e+03   OK    cond of the Hessian in the mode's own metric, a
                                                               standard deviation away. 1 means the posterior is
                                                               Gaussian in that metric; large means the curvature
                                                               varies and a fixed mass matrix cannot track it, so
                                                               HMC will struggle however long it is run
  distinct optima                     1            1   OK    over 5 solves that converged, from the mode
                                                               plus 4 dispersed restarts. More than one
                                                               means the mode found depends on the start
  --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  The mode check is "distance to the mode", NOT the gradient norm. ||grad log p|| carries the
  units of the log-density and of theta, and its floor is set by the working precision -- in
  float32 it bottoms out near 1e-2 on these problems and no absolute tolerance can be met.
  sqrt(g' H^-1 g) rescales it to posterior standard deviations, where < 0.01 means the mode is
  located to within a hundredth of one and nothing downstream is affected.

  parameter            MAP      post sd   sd/|MAP|   log p fall       at         verdict
  --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  theta[0]             0.19      0.02406      0.127          inf       --   OK    identified
  theta[1]          0.22432      0.08457      0.377        123.1   1e+00x   OK    identified
  theta[2]           2.9717      0.06787     0.0228          inf       --   OK    identified
  --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  state       GP lengthscale    grid dt    ell/dt  obs gap/dt         what it means
  --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  X[0]                  1.65      0.125     13.20         4.0   OK    smooth enough to constrain between observations
  X[1]                 1.562      0.125     12.50         4.0   OK    smooth enough to constrain between observations
  --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  The GP prior is all that holds the trajectory between observations, so a lengthscale short
  against the grid spacing lets it interpolate the data and do anything in between. This is
  set by the hyperparameter fit, before any inference, and is not something the posterior
  approximation can repair.

  "log p fall" is the drop in the profiled log-density on walking that parameter out to "at" times its
  own scale, with the states re-profiled at each step so the walk follows the ridge. Below
  3 nats the posterior is improper there. "at" is the furthest radius that resolved.

  STATUS: OK
    The mode is a unique maximum, every parameter is proper, and the GP constrains the states.
